---
source: tests/cli/basics.rs
expression: "format!(\"usage: {listed}\")"
---
usage: fetchloom [options] <command>

commands:
  add          add a dataset to the project and download it into the data folder
  remove       remove a dataset and the unchanged files fetchloom placed for it
  drop         leave files out of their dataset for good, such as bad samples
  sync         put the files data.lock lists into the data folder
  lock         update data.lock from data.toml, without changing the data folder
  build        run the recipes and record their results in data.lock
  status       list files that are missing, changed locally or extra
  list         list the project's datasets: source, size and folder
  export       write the SHA-256 or link of each file, for other tools
  push         copy the files data.lock lists into a folder mirror
  path         print where a dataset or a file in it is, syncing it if needed
  cache        show the cache, free what no project needs, or verify it
  settings     show each setting, its value and where it came from
  get          fetch something once, without a project
  search       find datasets on hugging face, kaggle and zenodo
  auth         sign in for private data, or data with terms to accept
  completions  print a script that completes fetchloom's commands in a shell
  help         explain the ideas behind fetchloom, or one command

options:
  -q, --quiet         print only the answer, warnings and errors
  -v, --verbose...    say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug logs
      --json          print one JSON document on stdout, not the usual output
      --progress      with --json, keep plain progress lines on stderr
      --offline       use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes           answer yes to questions, but never pick a dataset for you
      --color <when>  when to use color: auto, the default, always or never
  -C <dir>            run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
      --mirror <url>  ask the mirror at this web address or folder for files
                      before their sources. repeat it for more
      --no-config     leave the settings file unread for this run
  -h, --help          print help
  -V, --version       print the version

docs: https://nikhil-yn-aix.github.io/fetchloom
report a bug: https://github.com/nikhil-yn-aix/fetchloom/issues
